course: dictionary
lesson: 12211
title: Congruent: exactly the same
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Congruent means exactly the same shape and size. If you cut out one shape and place it on top of another, every edge and corner matches up perfectly.
explain: «The two triangles are congruent.» This tells you the triangles match exactly. You could turn one or flip it over, and it would still fit exactly on top of the other.
explain: Being congruent is not the same as looking alike. «These two squares are similar, but not congruent.» They have the same shape, but one is bigger, so they are not the same size.
fact: Congruent means the same shape and the same size.
fact: «Congruent» is an adjective. The noun is congruence.
fact: Congruent shapes can be turned, flipped or slid, and they are still congruent.
fact: In geometry, you can prove that two triangles are congruent with tests such as SSS, SAS and ASA.
fact: Similar shapes have the same shape but can be different sizes. Congruent shapes are always the same size too.
exercise: «The two triangles are congruent.» What does congruent mean here? | *Exactly the same shape and size | Same shape, but one is bigger | Pointing in the same direction | Same colour
exercise: Two squares each have sides of 4 cm. Are they congruent? | *Yes, they are the same shape and size | No, one is turned | No, one is a rectangle | No, they are different colours
exercise: «The shapes are similar but not congruent.» What must be true? | They are exactly the same size | They are both circles | They have different shapes and sizes | *They have the same shape, but are different sizes
test: Ben flips a triangle over and places it on another. It fits exactly. Are the triangles congruent? | No, only turning counts | *Yes, flipping does not change size or shape | Not sure, because flipping changes them
test: The noun from «congruent» is which word? | *Congruence | Congrument | Congruate | Congrue
exam: Which pair must be congruent? | *Two rectangles, both 3 cm by 5 cm, one turned round | Two rectangles, one 2 cm by 8 cm and one 3 cm by 5 cm | Two circles with different radii | Two triangles with the same angles but different sizes
